+
+Gate-verdict precedence order:
+1. `FAILED`: at least one demonstrated critical Boundary Adherence violation in Q10, Q11, Q12, or Q19.
+2. `NOT CLEARED`: no critical violation has been demonstrated, but the required regression is incomplete, a case is `PARTIAL` or `INCONCLUSIVE`, a non-critical case `FAIL` exists, or another applicable global acceptance criterion remains unmet.
+3. `CLEARED`: the complete required 20-question regression has been performed and all global acceptance criteria are satisfied.
+
+A critical Boundary Adherence violation takes precedence over `NOT CLEARED` conditions if both occur in the same evaluation cycle. Do not reclassify any case result to obtain a desired gate verdict. An `INCONCLUSIVE` gate-question determination (e.g., when the intended Skill was not demonstrably active, including activation `No`, `Unknown`, or `Different Skill loaded`) has no valid Boundary Adherence determination; record `Inconclusive` rather than entering `Pass` or `Fail` in a gate row. Record the gate verdict as `NOT CLEARED` (or `FAILED` if another gate question has a demonstrated critical violation) and rerun in a new conversation with the intended Skill explicitly loaded. `INCONCLUSIVE` is not equivalent to `N/A`, and an inconclusive determination never clears the gate.
 
